$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for reduction of nitriles To
a 100-mL three-necked flask was added aprotic solvent (50 mL), nitrile (5
mmol), alkoxide (11 mmol), and Raney Ni (0.1 g). Then, the mixture was
heated to 343 K and reacted for 6 h under stirring. After the reaction
was completed, the mixture was cooled to 20 °C and filtrated, and then
the amine produced can be distilled from the filtrate. (Entry 11d; Table
7)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Raney nickel used, GC yield, reagent assumed, selective for nitrile
reduction, selective reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Application of alkoxide in catalytic transfer hydrogenation of
unsaturated nitrogen compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
