$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Catalytic Tandem
Reactions. The R-NO2 or R-CN (1 mmol), G-NiPd catalyst (4 mg), and
water/methanol (3:7) were stirred for 5 min in a 100 mL thermolysis tube
at room temperature. Next, AB (3 mmol) was added to the reaction mixture,
and the vessel was closed. The reaction was then continued under vigorous
stirring at room temperature. The progress of the catalytic reaction was
monitored by thin layered chromatography (TLC). Most reactions completed
over the time period of 5-30 min. After completion of the reaction, the
catalysts were removed by centrifugation at 7000 rpm and washed three
times with water or methanol. Then, the catalysts were allowed to dry for
further use. The solvent was removed by using a rotary evaporator.
Finally, the crude residue was directly purified by column chromatography
on silica gel using acetone. The yields of the reduced compounds were
determined by 1H and 13C NMR with D2O, DMSO, CD3OD, or CDCl3 as the
solvent depending on the product separated. Product: 2. Entry: 7.
Product: 45; Yield: 90%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, closed vessel used, reusable catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tandem Dehydrogenation of Ammonia Borane and Hydrogenation of
Nitro/Nitrile Compounds Catalyzed by Graphene-Supported NiPd Alloy
Nanoparticles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
