$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for reduction of nitriles To
a 100-mL three-necked flask was added aprotic solvent (50 mL), nitrile (5
mmol), alkoxide (11 mmol), and Raney Ni (0.1 g). Then, the mixture was
heated to 343 K and reacted for 6 h under stirring. After the reaction
was completed, the mixture was cooled to 20 °C and filtrated, and then
the amine produced can be distilled from the filtrate.
(1H-indol-2-yl)methanamine (Entry 10; Table 7), Yield (89%) 1H NMR
(DMSO-d6, 400 MHz, ppm): δ = 3.84 (s, 2H), 6.22 (s, 1H), 6.93 (t, 1H, J =
8.0 Hz), 7.01 (t, 1H, J = 7.8 Hz), 7.30 (d, 1H, J = 7.8 Hz), 7.44 (d, 1H,
J = 8.0 Hz), 8.57 (s, 2H), 10.94 (brs, 1H); 13C NMR (DMSO-d6, 100 MHz,
ppm): δ = 57.4, 98.2, 111.1, 118.9, 119.6, 120.4, 128.5, 136.4, 141.8
[49].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Raney nickel used, selective for nitrile reduction, selective reaction
