$DATUM 60-29-7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: As an illustrative example of the
hydrogenation procedure, nitrile 1a (2.0 g, 24.1 mmol) was refluxed in a
magnetically stirred suspension of Raney nickel (5 g) in 2-propanol (30
mL) containing 2% KOH (w/v) for 1 h with the condenser open to the
atmosphere. After cooling to room temperature the organic layer was
decanted from the Raney nickel[27] and the catalyst was washed with
diethyl ether (3 x 10 mL). The combined organic layers were filtered
through Celite and concentrated by rotatory evaporation. The residue was
stirred with 10% HCl (20 mL) for 15 min to hydrolyze the N-isopropylidene
pentanamine. The reaction mixture was made basic with 10% KOH (10 mL),
cooled, and extracted with diethyl ether (4 x 20 mL). The combined ether
layers were dried (potassium carbonate), filtered, and concentrated by
rotatory evaporation. To this residue was added HCl in diethyl ether
(1.0M, 30mL). The mixture was concentrated by rotatory evaporation,
filtered, washed with cold diethyl ether and dried to give 2.88 g (97%)
of 4a as a white solid. The 1H and 13C NMR spectra and the mass spectra
of the free amine of 4a were identical to spectra of authentic
pentanamine. 4e, yield 88%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Transfer hydrogenation of nitriles with 2-propanol and Raney nickel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mebane, Robert C.; Jensen, David R.; Rickerd, Kerry R.; Gross, Benjamin
H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2003), 33(19), 3373-3379

