$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (33) General Procedure for the
[MeC(OH)2]+ClO4–-Catalyzed Synthesis of Amidoalkyl Naphthols A mixture of
an aldehyde (1 mmol), β-naphthol (1 mmol) with amide, nitrile, urea, or
carbamate (1 mmol) in the presence of [MeC(OH)2]+ClO4– (1 mol%) was
stirred in EtOAc (1 mL) at r.t. (or at 80 °C under solvent-free
conditions) for the given times. After completion of the reaction (TLC
monitoring), H2O was added, and the precipitate was filtered off to give
the corresponding amidoalkyl naphthols. Most of the products were known
and characterized by comparison of their melting points and spectral data
with those reported in the literature without further purification. In
some cases the products were recrystallized from EtOH–H2O (60:40).
N-[(2-Hydroxynaphthalen-1-yl)(phenyl)methyl]-benzamide, Yield 88% Obs. mp
(°C) 237–239, Lit. mp (°C) 239–2408. IR (KBr): νmax = 1625, 3065, 3418
cm–1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 7.20–7.90 (m, 16 H), 8.10–8.13 (d, 1
H, J = 8.4 Hz), 9.02 (d, 1 H, J = 8.4 Hz), 10.33 (s, 1 H, NH) ppm. 13C
NMR (75 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 50.0, 119.1, 119.4, 123.4, 127.1, 127.2,
127.5, 127.8, 128.9, 129.1, 129.2, 129.3, 130.1, 132.1, 133.0, 135.0,
142.7, 147.0, 153.9, 166.4 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, superacidic ionic liquid used as catalyst, catalyst
prepared and used, Ritter-type reaction, alternative preparation shown,
no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM [MeC(OH)2]+ClO4-: a new efficient organocatalyst for the preparation of
1-amido- and 1-carbamato-alkyl naphthols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Tamaddon, Fatemeh; Bistgani, Javad Moazeni
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2011), (20), 2947-2950

