$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for reduction of nitriles To
a 100-mL three-necked flask was added aprotic solvent (50 mL), nitrile (5
mmol), alkoxide (11 mmol), and Raney Ni (0.1 g). Then, the mixture was
heated to 343 K and reacted for 6 h under stirring. After the reaction
was completed, the mixture was cooled to 20 °C and filtrated, and then
the amine produced can be distilled from the filtrate. Benzylamine (Entry
6b; Table 7), Yield (85%) 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz, ppm): δ = 1.34 (s, 2H),
3.62 (s, 2H), 7.07–7.19 (m, 5H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz, ppm): δ = 46.2,
126.5, 126.9, 128.3, 143.4 [42].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Raney nickel used, selective for nitrile reduction and dechlorination,
selective reaction, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Application of alkoxide in catalytic transfer hydrogenation of
unsaturated nitrogen compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Xinzhi; Zhou, Shaodong; Chen, Yuehan; Dong, Zehan; Gao, Yeyu; Qian,
Chao; He, Chaohong
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Research on Chemical Intermediates (2012), 38(9), 2255-2269

