$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for preparation of amines
Under an argon atmosphere, the alkylated nitrile was added to a
suspension of lithium aluminum hydride (2 equivalents) in dry THF or
ether at 0°C. The mixture was stirred and brought to reflux for 3 hours,
before it was cooled in an ice-bath. A mixture of THF-water (5:1, v/v)
and then 15% aqueous sodium hydroxide solution was added dropwise to the
reaction mixture under vigorous stirring and cooling. After filtration
and washing with THF, the filtrate was concentrated under vacuum to
afford a colorless oil, which was purified by distillation.
2-ethyl-1-hex-5-enyl amine was prepared according to the general
procedure. Distillation of the crude product afforded the expected
product in 85% yield as a colorless oil. b.p.50°C (10 mmHg). 1H-NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): 0.84 (t, 3H), 1.26-1.35 (m, 5H), 1.50 (s, NH2), 1.96-2.07
(m, 2H), 2.58 (d, 2H, J =4.9 Hz), 4.87-5.02 (m, 2H), 5.71-5.84 (m, 1H).
13C-NMR (CDCl3): 11.0 (CH3), 23.7 (CH2), 34.8 (CH2), 35.7 (CH2), 42.3
(CH), 44.5 (CH2), 115.8 (=CH2), 137.0 (=CH).
